# Generated code
# Run `buf generate` from this directory to regenerate.
#
# /gen/go IS committed. Every Go service resolves the protobuf packages
# through `replace github.com/opus-casino/proto => ../../libs/proto`, so the
# import path github.com/opus-casino/proto/gen/go/<svc>/v1 only exists if the
# generated tree lives at ./gen/go. When it was ignored instead, CI checked out
# a module without those packages and every Go build, vet, test, lint and
# gosec job failed with "no required module provides package
# github.com/opus-casino/proto/gen/go/...". Regenerate with `make gen` and
# commit the result.
/gen/rust/
/gen/typescript/

